From 6a48878df951c3ec8462e21657ec99e7c4fb3e40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Woonggi Min <62207008+minpeter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:43:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] netprofm: Port reviewed dynamic connectivity and fault
 regressions to Soda.

Includes prerequisite IPv6 and loopback work by Hans Leidekker and Paul Gofman,
while retaining Valve prefer-native and ICMP behavior.

- Track NSI link, address and route notifications in netprofm; size netlink
  datagrams with MSG_PEEK | MSG_TRUNC and bind the kernel listener before
  publishing the NSI device.
- Preserve public empty/partial IPv6 route enumeration while adding a private
  strict table selector for NLM.
- Add an optional passive Linux NetworkManager reachability provider using
  runtime-loaded sd-bus on the monitor thread with a 1s protocol budget,
  250ms signal-storm coalescing, and non-activating queries.
- Dispatch COM sink notifications through the GIT with an IPropertyNotifySink
  relay fallback when the NLM event typelib proxy is unregistered, keeping
  relay and manager references alive across synchronous callbacks.
- Retain the initial adapter snapshot when NSI subscriptions or the initial
  refresh fail, and clean up disposable test prefixes on every exit path.
---
